{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_ALEywpHb26N0U0QUz240rGTI","content":"1\tCreated-GMT: 2026-11-03 03:30:00 GMT\n2\tCreated-Local: 2026-11-03 10:30:00 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n3\tCoding-Agent: agy (Gemini 4 Argon High)\n4\tSession-ID: not-applicable (orchestrator-dispatched, fresh session)\n5\t# Task: H3-1 — diagnose the two blocked kernel-gate fixtures\n6\t\n7\tRole: compiler/VM diagnostic engineer (agy)\n8\tReviewer/landing: the ZCode glm orchestrator seat; the architect reviews the root-cause packet and any acceptance-budget change.\n9\t\n10\t## Governing instructions\n11\t\n12\tThe hardening-3 plan (approved) authorizes this slice: diagnose the two blocked fixtures of the slice-9 kernel differential gate. Read `test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_gate.md`, `test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_evidence.edn` (the blocked rows), and the harness `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj` (`kernel-row`, `kernel-c`, `run-guest-machine`, the instruction budget at `:instruction-budget-per-lane 2000000`). Work in `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-h31`, branch `hardening3-h3-1`, base `0805a2535` (master). You MAY run shell commands and tests — that is why you are on this lane. Push the branch when done; do NOT merge.\n13\t\n14\t## The state\n15\t\n16\tThe gate runs 106 fixtures: 100 pass, 2 are recorded deviations, 2 are recorded upstream failures, and **2 are blocked**:\n17\t\n18\t- `check-accepted` — only the **c-walker** lane blocks; the c-semantic lane COMPLETES.\n19\t- `check-assume-have-discharge` — **both C lanes** block.\n20\t\n21\tA and B complete for both. All three blocked C executions report \"Guest instruction budget exhausted\" at 2,000,000 steps. Blocked fixtures are not accepted negatives; the gate cannot close while they block.\n22\t\n23\t## The diagnostic packet (the deliverable)\n24\t\n25\tA four-cell comparison — each fixture on each C evaluator (walker/semantic) — containing:\n26\t\n27\t1. Pinned source/compiler/runtime identities, instrumentation mode, configured budget, ACTUAL steps consumed, terminal reason, and elapsed time per cell.\n28\t2. Aggregate cost and phase boundaries: loading/setup versus fixture execution. Check specifically whether the observer runner resets its step counter across consumer invocations — do not assume the reported count is a whole-fixture total.\n29\t3. Bounded snapshots at exhaustion: control position, continuation depth, call frequencies, and the ordered tail of the executed-call/trace stream (bounded — no full dumps).\n30\t4. Instrumented versus uninstrumented results, including the completing semantic run of `check-accepted` (what does the semantic lane see that the walker does not?).\n31\t5. A minimal reproduction if the evidence shows repeated admission, invocation, or continuation activity (a loop, a re-entrant helper, an unbounded recursion the budget masks).\n32\t\n33\tCollect diagnostics through the test harness's own facilities (the machine's streams, `:executed-calls`, continuation inspection). Do NOT recursively serialize host sessions or entire closure environments. Partial traces are diagnostic evidence only and contribute ZERO coverage.\n34\t\n35\t## Budget trials (authorized, bounded)\n36\t\n37\tFinite diagnostic trials at **2M, 4M, and 8M instructions**, stopping when sufficient evidence is obtained. These are diagnostic configurations, NOT an acceptance-budget change: before any budget raise is proposed, return measured completion costs, instrumentation overhead, progress evidence, and a proposed finite bound with justified headroom. Do not add retries that increase fuel until a fixture passes.\n38\t\n39\t## Boundaries\n40\t\n41\t- The fixtures, IDs, inputs, and expected A/B results are fixed; diagnostic reproductions supplement them.\n42\t- No changes to `yang.call`, `yin.vm`, or any `src/cljc/` source: if the evidence implicates the Clojure lowering, report the exact site and mechanism (a fix is a follow-up round after the architect reviews the packet); if it implicates the shared runtime, return the minimized reproduction for a ruling.\n43\t- No suppression of the blocked status, no accepted-negative claims, no coverage credit from diagnostic runs.\n44\t\n45\t## Verification and report\n46\t\n47\tRun the focused gate test (`clojure -M:test -v yang.latte-oracle-test/test-kernel-differential-gate`) before and after your diagnostic harness changes (if any) to show no regression: before = exactly 1 failure (the blocked assertion); after = the same, unless your packet explains a difference. clj-kondo on any touched file: 0 errors. The report goes in `docs/` beside the gate records or the round findings file — state the root-cause hypothesis ranked by evidence, the four-cell table, the trial results, and the recommended next round (harness fix / compiler fix / budget proposal / shared-runtime ruling request)."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_HZEkR4VYq4eSPsb8h6NRKlbZ","content":"1000\t            (throw e)))))))\n1001\t\n1002\t\n1003\t(defn- av-let\n1004\t  \"(let [p0 (data/nth av 0) ...] body): positional parameters of one arity.\n1005\t   A body that recurs is a loop over the same bindings: one recur target per\n1006\t   arity. Under the outcome model the body is lowered first.\"\n1007\t  [env macro-env params body-forms]\n1008\t  (let [bindings (into [] (mapcat (fn [i p] [p (list 'data/nth av-sym i)]) (range) params))\n1009\t        lowered? (outcomes? env)\n1010\t        body (if lowered?\n1011\t               (lower-function-body env macro-env params body-forms)\n1012\t               (body-expression body-forms))]\n1013\t    (if (some mentions-recur? body-forms)\n1014\t      (with-meta (if lowered?\n1015\t                   (list 'loop bindings body)\n1016\t                   (list* 'loop bindings body-forms))\n1017\t        {::fn-loop true})\n1018\t      (list 'let bindings body))))\n1019\t\n1020\t\n1021\t(defn- av-dispatch\n1022\t  \"Nested ifs over the argument vector's count, one branch per arity\n1023\t   {:n count :form branch}. An unmatched count falls through to a\n1024\t   zero-argument data/count, which the data module refuses with :reason\n1025\t   :arity; under the outcome model it is an arity error outcome naming\n1026\t   `fn-name` (or the anonymous fn's `source`) instead.\"\n1027\t  [env fn-name source arities]\n1028\t  (let [counts (map :n arities)]\n1029\t    (when (not= (count counts) (count (set counts)))\n1030\t      (reject! \"Two arities with the same parameter count\" {:counts (vec counts)}))\n1031\t    (reduce (fn [else {:keys [n form]}]\n1032\t              (list 'if\n1033\t                    (list 'data/content= (list 'data/count av-sym) n)\n1034\t                    form\n1035\t                    else))\n1036\t            (if (outcomes? env) (arity-error-form fn-name source) (list 'data/count))\n1037\t            (reverse arities))))\n1038\t\n1039\t\n1040\t(defn- check-av-params!\n1041\t  [params]\n1042\t  (when-not (vector? params)\n1043\t    (reject! \"fn parameters must be a vector\" {:params params}))\n1044\t  (doseq [p params]\n1045\t    (when (= '& p)\n1046\t      (reject! \"Variadic fn parameters are not supported\" {:params params}))\n1047\t    (check-binder! p params)))\n1048\t\n1049\t\n1050\t(defn- outcome-node\n1051\t  [tag value]\n1052\t  (u/app (u/v 'conj) (u/app (u/v 'conj) (u/lit []) (u/lit tag)) value))\n1053\t\n1054\t\n1055\t(defn- call-entry\n1056\t  \"The unary public entry, closed over a private argument-vector body.\"\n1057\t  []\n1058\t  (let [body (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"body\"))\n1059\t        invocation (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"invocation\"))\n1060\t        outcome (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"entry_outcome\"))\n1061\t        positional (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation) (u/lit :yang.call/positional))\n1062\t        named (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation) (u/lit :yang.call/named))\n1063\t        raise (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation) (u/lit :yang.call/raise))\n1064\t        binding-error (outcome-node\n1065\t                        error-tag\n1066\t                        (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/lit {})\n1067\t                               (u/lit :yin.k/message)\n1068\t                               (u/lit \"Clojure functions do not accept named arguments\")\n1069\t                               (u/lit :yin.k/data)\n1070\t                               (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/lit {})\n1071\t                                      (u/lit :yang.call/named) named)))\n1072\t        entry-body (u/let1\n1073\t                     outcome\n1074\t                     (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'dsg__empty) named)\n1075\t                                (u/app (u/v body) positional)\n1076\t                                binding-error)\n1077\t                     (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'dsg__equal)\n1078\t                                       (u/app (u/v 'data/nth) (u/v outcome) (u/lit 0))\n1079\t                                       (u/lit ok-tag))\n1080\t                                (u/app (u/v 'data/nth) (u/v outcome) (u/lit 1))\n1081\t                                (u/app raise\n1082\t                                       (u/app (u/v 'yang.call/thrown)\n1083\t                                              (u/app (u/v 'data/nth)\n1084\t                                                     (u/v outcome) (u/lit 1))))))\n1085\t        ;; The private lane forwards the body's outcome in tail position.\n1086\t        ;; The public entry still converts outcomes to value/raise normally.\n1087\t        entry (u/lam [invocation]\n1088\t                     (u/if-node\n1089\t                       (u/app (u/v 'dsg__equal)\n1090\t                              (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation)\n1091\t                                     (u/lit :clj/outcome-token))\n1092\t                              (u/v 'dsg__call_token))\n1093\t                       (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'dsg__empty) named)\n1094\t                                  (u/app (u/v body) positional)\n1095\t                                  binding-error)\n1096\t                       entry-body))]\n1097\t    (u/lam [body] entry)))\n1098\t\n1099\t\n1100\t(defn- admit-call-descriptor\n1101\t  \"Admit a descriptor constructed by trusted UAST/profile code. This is not\n1102\t   a source form: entry-spelled source maps never pass through this constructor.\"\n1103\t  [descriptor-ast tail?]\n1104\t  (let [descriptor-name 'dsg__descriptor\n1105\t        canonical (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) descriptor-ast\n1106\t                         (u/lit :clj/admission) (u/lit nil))\n1107\t        ;; The factory closure captures the canonical descriptor and private\n1108\t        ;; token. Projection reconstructs and compares that opaque closure;\n1109\t        ;; it never applies a source-supplied predicate. An equal immutable\n1110\t        ;; reconstruction i